00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:28.074
B3 star - how do you prevent identity spoofing between gateway and services.

414
00:15:28.354 --> 00:15:30.487
Y to T: start 30 seconds.

415
00:15:30.767 --> 00:15:36.677
Y to Y: answer aloud - mTLS identities, signed tokens, no trust in headers.

416
00:15:36.957 --> 00:15:39.453
Y to B: reveal 30-second answer.

417
00:15:39.733 --> 00:15:42.591
Y to Y: compare - missed token audience checks.

418
00:15:42.871 --> 00:15:45.666
Y to C: read the deep answer and follow-ups.

419
00:15:45.946 --> 00:15:48.677
Y to B: mark as miss - comes back tomorrow.

420
00:15:52.527 --> 00:15:54.873
Sequence: a follow-up chain in an interview.

421
00:15:55.153 --> 00:15:57.948
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

422
00:15:58.228 --> 00:16:00.916
I to C: how would you avoid double charges.

423
00:16:01.196 --> 00:16:05.612
C to I: idempotency key per payment attempt, stored with the result.

424
00:16:05.892 --> 00:16:09.263
I to C: two requests with the same key arrive at once.

425
00:16:09.543 --> 00:16:13.703
C to I: unique constraint, second waits or gets the stored result.

426
00:16:13.983 --> 00:16:16.009
I to C: gateway times out.

427
00:16:16.289 --> 00:16:21.559
C to I: outcome unknown - query status with the same key, never retry blind.

428
00:16:21.839 --> 00:16:24.569
I to C: status API is down too.

429
00:16:24.849 --> 00:16:31.292
C to I: saga stays pending, sweeper retries, reconciliation with settlement files as the backstop.

